---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Anasazi Restaurant",
  servesCuisine: ["Southwestern", "American"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-505-988-3030",
  url: "https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/inn-of-the-anasazi-santa-fe/dining",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "113 Washington Ave",
    addressLocality: "Santa Fe",
    addressRegion: "NM",
    postalCode: "87501",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Anasazi Restaurant at Rosewood Inn of the Anasazi, Santa Fe — refined Southwestern fine dining under executive chef Cristian Pontiggia, one block from the Plaza.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Anasazi Restaurant Menu Guide (2026) — Rosewood Inn of the Anasazi, Santa Fe | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to Anasazi Restaurant at Rosewood Inn of the Anasazi, Santa Fe: hours, signature dishes, official menu prices, and reservations."
  path="/anasazi-restaurant-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/anasazi-restaurant-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/anasazi-restaurant-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a refined contemporary Southwestern fine-dining room with adobe tones, a sculptural kiva fireplace, Native-inspired modern art and white tablecloths at dusk (illustrative, not the actual restaurant)"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Santa Fe, NM
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Anasazi Restaurant — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Anasazi Restaurant is the dining room of <strong>Rosewood Inn of the
      Anasazi</strong> at 113 Washington Avenue, a block from the Plaza — the most
      decorated hotel dining room in Santa Fe. Executive chef <strong>Cristian
      Pontiggia</strong> (with chef de cuisine Oliver Cortez) cooks refined
      Southwestern food in an adobe room of viga beams and Native textiles: bison
      carpaccio, the famous mushroom cappuccino, Akaushi beef tenderloin. Unlike
      most peers, the restaurant's official site carries a real priced menu —
      though it's the in-room dining menu, so the dining-room figures may differ.
      Everything is written in our own words.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">113 Washington Ave, Santa Fe, NM 87501 (Rosewood Inn of the Anasazi, one block from the Plaza)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Executive chef Cristian Pontiggia; chef de cuisine Oliver Cortez (per Rosewood)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Refined Southwestern</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">$$$$ — official menu: starters $19–$23, mains $29–$35 (current, in-room menu)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Via Rosewood (Make an Inquiry) or 505-988-3030</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Recognition</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Rosewood calls it "award-winning" — no specific public award named</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Hours</h2>
      <p>
        Per current listings (October 2026): the restaurant and bar run
        <strong>daily 7:00 AM–10:00 PM</strong>; the lunch–dinner menu runs
        <strong>11:00 AM–9:00 PM</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Signature dishes</h2>
      <p>
        The dishes Rosewood and its guests keep naming:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Mushroom cappuccino</strong>: the famous one — the dish reviewers call unmissable.</li>
        <li><strong>Bison carpaccio</strong>: the signature starter, per Rosewood's own copy.</li>
        <li><strong>Akaushi beef tenderloin</strong>: the prestige cut.</li>
        <li><strong>Silver Coin margarita</strong>: the signature cocktail.</li>
        <li><strong>Pear carpaccio</strong>: a lighter signature.</li>
        <li><strong>Citrus tres leches cake</strong>: the dessert guests photograph.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official prices (current, in-room dining menu)</h2>
      <p>
        These are the restaurant's own figures from the official menu on
        rosewoodhotels.com — <strong>current as of our October 2026 check</strong>.
        One honest flag: this is the <strong>in-room dining menu</strong>; the main
        dining room's menu may carry different items and prices, so confirm when you book:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Starters:</strong> pico and guacamole $21; tortilla soup (roasted corn, asadero) $21; "Not a Caesar" salad $19; jamón serrano $23.</li>
        <li><strong>Mains:</strong> Anasazi Cobb salad $29 (add chicken $10, shrimp $14); Anasazi smash burger $29 (add bacon $9); tuna poke $29; tuna carpaccio $35; New Mexican sandwich $29.</li>
        <li><strong>Dessert:</strong> dark chocolate tart $22.</li>
        <li><strong>Drinks:</strong> coffee $9–$10; juices $9.</li>
        <li><strong>Special events:</strong> the September 25, 2026 Wine &amp; Chile Fiesta dinner with Hundred Acre wines was listed at CAD 695 per person.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one dinner here, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Start with:</strong> the mushroom cappuccino — it's the legend.</li>
        <li><strong>The splurge:</strong> the bison carpaccio followed by the Akaushi tenderloin.</li>
        <li><strong>The drink:</strong> the Silver Coin margarita.</li>
        <li><strong>Finish:</strong> the citrus tres leches cake.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Reserve ahead</strong> — via the Rosewood site's inquiry form or 505-988-3030; this is a small, popular room.</li>
        <li><strong>Prices are official but in-room-menu era:</strong> the figures above come from the official in-room menu; ask about the dining room's current menu when you book.</li>
        <li><strong>Wine &amp; Chile Fiesta:</strong> Anasazi hosts ticketed wine dinners during Santa Fe's September fiesta — they sell out.</li>
        <li><strong>The tequila table:</strong> the hotel's exclusive tequila experience is worth asking about.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/inn-of-the-anasazi-santa-fe/dining" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official dining page — Rosewood Inn of the Anasazi</a> (restaurant info, reservations inquiry)</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/inn-of-the-anasazi-santa-fe/dining/anasazi-restaurant/anasazi-restaurant-menu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official menu page — Anasazi Restaurant</a> (priced menu, event menus)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        The figures above are <strong>official and current</strong> (checked October
        2026) — but they come from the restaurant's <strong>in-room dining
        menu</strong> on rosewoodhotels.com. The main dining room may serve a
        different menu at different prices. Always verify with the restaurant
        before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related guides -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">More New Mexico guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/best-hotel-restaurants-new-mexico/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">The best hotel restaurants in New Mexico →</a></li>
        <li><a href="/la-plazuela-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">La Plazuela</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— the landmark Southwestern room at La Fonda on the Plaza</span></li>
        <li><a href="/terra-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Terra</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Four Seasons Rancho Encantado's mountain-view dining room</span></li>
        <li><a href="/julia-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Julia</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Southwestern comfort in a Victorian mansion at La Posada</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
